Z||000000||Pretender||03-03-2000||06:01 PM||||One bottle of V-8 Splash per six-pack drank. I will drink this before I go to bed or if for some reason beyond my control I don't get to drink anymore liquids before I fall asleep I'll drink it as soon as I wake up in the morning. I've also used Gatoraid but I prefer the taste of the fruit drink better. Anyone else have a cure?<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Phil||03-03-2000||06:59 PM||||Sure fire cure<P>don't drink <BR>  I thought that one up all by myself.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||03-03-2000||08:45 PM||||Many years ago I was reading the articles in one of those magazines that people usualy only look at the pictures.  It had a sure fire cowboy cure. The morning after a roudy evening, the cowboys used to break the ice from the water tank and dunk their head in untill they couldn't stand it any longer.  After that in the mornings I would stand in the shower and turn on the COLD water untill I couldn't breath (wife was never in the mood the next morning anyway).  It worked for me and I also learned not to drink that much anymore either.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||03-03-2000||09:04 PM||||2 excedrins, a <B>HUGE</B> bowl of popcorn, a 2 liter of RC, the remote and the couch, usually work best for me <P>if that doesnt work, then i start drinking again... a fith of hera dura tequila will make you forget about anything  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spyder||03-03-2000||09:51 PM||||Take a large glass of water and drink four aspirin. LOL<BR>Don't forget to eat at Waffel House before passing out!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||03-03-2000||11:57 PM||||A great big bowl of Menudo, heavy on the chilis!  Nothing like a stomach full of spicy cow stomach to clean out the system. Best if washed down with a cold bud light and plenty of tortillas.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||03-04-2000||06:03 AM||||Actually, lots of vitamin B12 will help.  That's what's in V8 juice (the tomato juice is what does the trick).  I know of a couple of drunks that make a special trip to the doctors office every once in a while to get a B12 shot.  It must help.  I've never seen them with a hangover.||||reg||1
Z||000007||olympic||03-04-2000||04:37 PM||||A BIG part of a hangover is dehydration (alchol absorbes water) Drinking a couple glasses of water before going to sleep is suppose to help.  Also, waiting till you've sobered up a little before passing out helps.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||03-05-2000||12:00 AM||||When you get into bed, stick one leg out from under the covers and put your foot on the floor. Stops the bed from spinning. <BR>All kidding aside... I try to take a couple of aspirin (NEVER take Tylenol when there is a lot of alcohol in your system), and drink a glass of water or two. I also try to eat something.   ||||reg||1
Z||000009||loafer87gt||03-05-2000||01:16 PM||||Like M onkeyMan asid, take some Vitamin B pills before you hit the sheets. A hangover is caused by the depletion of Vitamin B in your brain. Me and four of my buddies managed to kill a full keg of beer in a day and a half over spring break and didn't suffer from any hangover at all. Proof that it works.||||reg||1
